\subsection{Experiment 4: Behavioural Aggregation (\texttt{agg\_eg.ipynb}, \texttt{agg\_music.ipynb})}
\label{sec:behavioural_agg}

The behavioural aggregation approach (\Cref{sec:profile_aggregation}) builds a profile vector per \globalentity{} and runs a second \splink{} layer.

\subsubsection{MusicBrainz Profile Construction}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \texttt{artist} as global ID.
    \item Numerical: length mean/min/max $\to$ range overlap comparison.
    \item Categorical sets: title, album, language $\to$ frequency vectors $\to$ magnitude-weighted cosine.
    \item Set fields: track number $\to$ Simpson; year $\to$ exact overlap count.
    \item Blocking on track number intersection $\ge 1$.
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection{Second-Layer \splink{} Results}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Comparison: Soft Jaccard (title), Monge-Elkan (title), Year overlap, Simpson (track number), Range overlap (length).
    \item \emalgo{} with 4 training rules (track exact, length overlap, year overlap, title soft Jaccard).
    \item Match weight chart: \textit{TBD: insert visualisation}.
    \item Precision-Recall: \textit{TBD: compare against single-layer baseline}.
\end{itemize}

